{
  "$readme": [
    "THE SCHEMA CONTRACT \u2014 what every tool's schema must keep KNOWABLE.",
    "",
    "The catalog is injected into every request, so its schema is a permanent",
    "cost \u2014 and a permanent instruction. Compressing it is right; losing a",
    "fact in it is not.",
    "",
    "This file separates the two:",
    "",
    "  - the STRUCTURE (properties, enums, required, annotations, and the",
    "    per-action routing tables) is pinned EXACTLY. A change there is a",
    "    contract change, and it must be made deliberately.",
    "",
    "  - the FACTS are pinned SEMANTICALLY. Each is a regex that must still",
    "    match the argument's description, so a description can be reworded",
    "    or shortened as long as the fact it carried survives. A fact that",
    "    disappears, or a description that does without it, fails here.",
    "",
    "THE ROUTING MAP IS GENERATED, NOT WRITTEN. The tool description carries",
    "one `Args by action \u2014 ...` line built from the SAME `*_ACTION_ARGS`",
    "tables the handlers use. It replaces ~50 hand-written parentheticals",
    "scattered across the arguments, and it makes a class of drift",
    "structurally impossible: the hand-written ones had already drifted",
    "(`archgen_docs.collection` claimed one action and belongs to six).",
    "",
    "packages/mcp/test/protocol/schema-routing.test.mjs checks all of it."
  ],
